{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The frozen check passed. The capture includes many annexed image files, so I’m narrowing the manifest review to identity, HEAD, reference limits, and scientific artifact paths rather than dumping the full file inventory. I’ll now read the item rules and response schema, then inspect only the delivered project files and their provenance."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_VERSION\")/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- runner help ---\\\\n'\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" --help\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- relevant manifest summary ---\\\\n'\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\nfor name in ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST','STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST']:\n d=json.load(open(os.environ[name]))\n print(name, 'capture_sha256=',d.get('capture_sha256') or d.get('sha256'), 'head=',d.get('head'), 'keys=',list(d)[:20])\nfor p in [os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET']),'judge-target.json'),os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']]:\n d=json.load(open(p)); print('\\\\n',p)\n for k,v in d.items():\n  if k in ['reference_limits','head','captured_head','delivery_capture_sha256','commit','git','worker','capture','capture_identity','target']:\n   print(k, json.dumps(v)[:3000])\nPY\nprintf '\\\\n--- target top-level ---\\\\n'\nfind \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -maxdepth 3 -mindepth 1 ! -path '\"'*/.git/*' \"'! -path '\"'*/.git/annex/*' -print | sort | head -250\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_VERSION\")/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- runner help ---\\\\n'\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" --help\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- relevant manifest summary ---\\\\n'\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\nfor name in ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST','STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST']:\n d=json.load(open(os.environ[name]))\n print(name, 'capture_sha256=',d.get('capture_sha256') or d.get('sha256'), 'head=',d.get('head'), 'keys=',list(d)[:20])\nfor p in [os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET']),'judge-target.json'),os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']]:\n d=json.load(open(p)); print('\\\\n',p)\n for k,v in d.items():\n  if k in ['reference_limits','head','captured_head','delivery_capture_sha256','commit','git','worker','capture','capture_identity','target']:\n   print(k, json.dumps(v)[:3000])\nPY\nprintf '\\\\n--- target top-level ---\\\\n'\nfind \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -maxdepth 3 -mindepth 1 ! -path '\"'*/.git/*' \"'! -path '\"'*/.git/annex/*' -print | sort | head -250\"","aggregated_output":"# Scientific assessment context\n\nAssess the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: a positive parametric effect of potential gain in vmPFC for the equal-indifference group.\nThe original [analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf) require whole-brain-corrected inference.\nThe scientific task is in `input/study-task.md`.\n\nWorkers receive 54 participant gain-effect maps from team AO86 and the corresponding cohort metadata.\nPreprocessing and participant modeling are fixed; evaluate group inference conditional on those inputs.\nJudge whether the analysis handles the intended participants, image geometry, quality, gain scaling, uncertainty and anatomical interpretation appropriately.\nThe maps represent independent participants; runs have already been combined within each person.\nEvaluate exclusions, uncertainty and multiple-comparison correction against the actual method.\nDefensible approaches can reach different conclusions; matching a prior team's answer is not the criterion.\nKeep scientific validity separate from the frozen STAMPED assessment.\nCheck how image coverage and missing observations enter the analysis; whether spatial alignment, vmPFC definition, group-model assumptions and whole-brain correction support the claimed inference; and whether quality checks, uncertainty and figures make those decisions inspectable.\nDo not require a particular mask, atlas, model or numerical result.\nParticipant variance maps are absent; judge methods against the supplied data.\n\n--- runner help ---\nusage: assessment.py [-h] {check,probes,response,validate,fresh-rerun} ...\n\nRun the pinned assessment helpers in their recorded Pixi environment.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {check,probes,response,validate,fresh-rerun}\n  arguments\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n\n--- relevant manifest summary ---\nSTAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST capture_sha256= None head= None keys= ['capture_finished_at', 'capture_status', 'captured_at', 'declared_artifacts', 'entries', 'errors', 'git_dependencies', 'git_metadata', 'head_commit', 'kind', 'omissions', 'policy', 'schema', 'workspace']\nSTAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST capture_sha256= None head= None keys= ['capture_finished_at', 'capture_status', 'captured_at', 'declared_artifacts', 'entries', 'errors', 'git_dependencies', 'git_metadata', 'head_commit', 'kind', 'omissions', 'policy', 'schema', 'workspace']\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 6, in <module>\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/judge-target.json'\n\n--- target top-level ---\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.codex\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.codex/hooks.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire/.gitignore\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire/logs\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire/logs/entire.log\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire/metadata\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire/metadata/01a1438a-ba02-7fa0-9329-054220d14179\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspace/.entire/settings.local.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-05-j02/operational/content/workspa