{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'find \"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\")\")\" -maxdepth 4 -type f -name '\"'judge-target.json' -print\nfind \\\"\"'$(dirname \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\")\" -maxdepth 4 -type f ! -path '\"'*/annex/*' -printf '%P\\\\n' | sort | tail -100\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/REPORT.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- protocol ---\\\\n'\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/protocol.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- scripts ---\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,260p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/scripts/group_analysis.py\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- run entry/retriever ---\\\\n'\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/run_analysis.sh\"\nsed -n '\"'1,220p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/scripts/retrieve_maps.py\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'find \"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\")\")\" -maxdepth 4 -type f -name '\"'judge-target.json' -print\nfind \\\"\"'$(dirname \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\")\" -maxdepth 4 -type f ! -path '\"'*/annex/*' -printf '%P\\\\n' | sort | tail -100\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/REPORT.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- protocol ---\\\\n'\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/protocol.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- scripts ---\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,260p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/scripts/group_analysis.py\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n--- run entry/retriever ---\\\\n'\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/run_analysis.sh\"\nsed -n '\"'1,220p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/scripts/retrieve_maps.py\"'","aggregated_output":"find: -printf: unknown primary or operator\n# Potential monetary gain and brain activity\n\n## Result\n\n**The supplied maps do not support a positive vmPFC gain effect in the NARPS equal-indifference group.** In a coordinate-defined vmPFC display box (MNI x = −12 to 12, y = 30 to 55, z = −15 to 10 mm), the across-participant mean contrast was −0.0035 (95% CI −0.0229 to 0.0160; arbitrary upstream units). No voxel in this box survived the one-sided whole-brain family-wise error (FWE) test. The interval includes zero and is not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\n\nThe whole-brain analysis did identify 24 positive voxels in three small posterior islands after maximum-t FWE correction (54 participants, 198,029 voxels, 9,999 sign flips, p<sub>FWE</sub> ≤ .05). The strongest voxel was at MNI (−26, −102, −3.6) mm (mean contrast 0.1121, t(53)=6.62, p<sub>FWE</sub>=.0006). This location is far posterior to vmPFC and does not support the stated regional hypothesis. Parametric voxelwise Bonferroni, a conservative reference analysis, retained 11 positive voxels, also outside the vmPFC box.\n\n![Participant vmPFC summaries and whole-brain t slices; purple outlines mark voxels passing whole-brain max-t FWE p ≤ .05. The green dashed box marks the vmPFC display region.](figures/group_results.png)\n\n## Methods and interpretation\n\nThe sample was the complete supplied set of 54 equal-indifference participants (age 21–37 years; 30 F, 24 M); no participants were excluded. The unit of analysis was the participant. We fit a voxelwise one-sample t model to the unthresholded participant gain-effect maps, testing the directional alternative that the population mean is greater than zero. The common analysis mask contained voxels with nonzero image support in every map. Positive one-sided maximum-t permutation inference used participant-level sign flips and controls voxelwise whole-brain FWE without a spatial-smoothness model. Its null assumes participant effects are symmetric around zero. The permutation p-value used the plus-one estimate. A coordinate box was used only to describe vmPFC; it did not constrain the whole-brain search or determine the corrected inference. vmPFC has multiple anatomical definitions, so the box is an explicit display approximation rather than a universal atlas boundary.\n\nThese are participant contrast parameter estimates for a mean-centered, variance-normalized gain modulator, averaged across four runs by the fixed upstream AO86 model. They are neither z/t statistics nor a response change per currency unit. In particular, the task’s gain range being twice its loss range does not make this coefficient a per-dollar sensitivity. The gain and loss modulators were fit in separate models; inference is conditional on that modeling decision.\n\n## Uncertainty and limits\n\nThe group analysis is unweighted because participant variance maps and the complete executable upstream pipeline are unavailable. Thus the test measures between-participant variation in supplied point estimates and does not propagate each participant’s first-level uncertainty. Sign-flip inference also relies on symmetry under the null. No significant vmPFC voxel means this analysis did not establish a positive vmPFC effect under its whole-brain-corrected criterion; it does not show the effect is absent, and it does not rule out a smaller effect, an effect defined by another anatomical boundary, or uncertainty induced upstream. The vmPFC box interval is relatively broad and should not be read as an equivalence test.\n\n## Reproduction and supporting files\n\nRun `bash run_analysis.sh` from this directory. It retrieves only the 54 manifest-listed NeuroVault participant maps, checks each byte count and SHA-256 against `input/sources.json`, and runs the group model. The provided common Python environment is used by default.\n\n- [Protocol and method revision record](protocol.md)\n- [Group analysis code](scripts/group_analysis.py), [input retrieval and checksum verification](scripts/retrieve_maps.py), [runner](run_analysis.sh)\n- [Machine-readable results](results/summary.json), [whole-brain corrected clusters](results/fwe_clusters.csv), [participant QC](results/participant_qc.csv), [retrieval checksums](results/retrieval-manifest.txt)\n- [Analysis and input SHA-256 records](results/code-input-sha256.txt)\n- [Mean, t and max-t corrected p maps](results/group_mean.nii.gz), [t map](results/group_t.nii.gz), [corrected p map](results/group_p_fwe_max_t.nii.gz)\n- [Figure source and rendering](figures/group_results.svg), [PNG](figures/group_results.png)\n- [Fixed upstream methods](input/upstream-methods.md), [data/source manifest](input/sources.json), [cohort metadata](input/participants.tsv)\n\nNumerical checks matched SciPy’s independent one-sample t test at the three strongest voxels and for a complete independent sign-flip t-map/max-stat calculation (maximum absolute t difference recorded in `results/summary.json`). Inputs were checked against all manifest hashes before analysis. The [original NARPS analysis instructions (Hypothesis 1)](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf) were provided as the study source; retrieval through the reference browser timed out during this run, so its full text was not independently inspected here.\n\n--- protocol ---\n# Analysis protocol\n\nQuestion: among the 54 equal-indifference NARPS participants, do supplied gain-modulator contrast estimates have a positive group mean in brain locations anatomically corresponding to vmPFC?\n\n## Fixed inputs and estimand\n\nUse exactly the 54 participant maps listed in `input/sources.json` and the matching rows in `input/participants.tsv`. Each NIfTI is an unthresholded participant gain-effect estimate, averaged over four runs in MNI152NLin2009cAsym. It estimates a coefficient for a mean-centered, variance-normalized gain modulator, not a currency-unit slope or a standardized statistic. Upstream preprocessing and individual models are fixed; no time series are retrieved. The group estimand is the one-sample mean participant contrast at each voxel for this selected group.\n\n## Primary group model and inference\n\nAt each voxel, estimate the one-sample mean and standard error across independent participant maps and test the directional alternative mean > 0 with a one-sample t statistic (df=53). Use an explicit common finite-data analysis mask derived from voxels covered by every map. Primary whole-brain family-wise correction uses the maximum positive t across 9,999 participant-level sign-flip permutations (seed 20261016); it requires symmetry of participant effects under the null and preserves each participant as the sampling unit. The p-value uses the plus-one correction. Parametric voxelwise Bonferroni is also retained as a conservative reference that does not rely on spatial smoothness. The support criterion is a positive whole-brain-corrected voxel in an anatomically plausible vmPFC location; a subthreshold result is not evidence of no effect. Report the map-based mean contrast and t statistic, without interpreting coefficient magnitude in dollars.\n\n## Checks and exclusions\n\nVerify input SHA-256 and byte counts against the supplied manifest; enforce unique IDs and exact set match to metadata; inspect affine, shape, voxel sizes, finite coverage and per-map summary distributions. Exclude no participant for statistical extremity; only structural or nonfinite failures could exclude a map, reported individually. No covariates are included: age/gender are not needed for this group mean and would change the estimand. Report the overlap mask size, all exclusions and the non-parametric upstream limitations (participant variance maps unavailable; gain and loss were fit separately).\n\n## Validation and deliverables\n\nCross-check voxelwise t and one-sided p-values against SciPy's independent one-sample t-test on selected voxels and summarize a coordinate-defined vmPFC display box separately from whole-brain inference. Generate checked table and NIfTI outputs, editable plotting code, figures and execution/environment records. No sensitivity result replaces the primary result.\n\n## Protocol revision record\n\nThe initial written protocol proposed voxelwise Bonferroni correction as primary. Before accepting the final run, this was revised to sign-flip maximum-t FWE as primary because the participant-level maps permit a direct sampling-unit resampling test with whole-brain max-statistic control. Bonferroni remains a reference analysis. The coordinate-defined vmPFC box is descriptive, not used to select the whole-brain inference. This amendment is reported as an analysis choice, not a prespecified design feature.\n\n--- scripts ---\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"One-sample gain-effect group analysis with whole-brain max-t sign flips.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport platform\nimport sys\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport nibabel as nib\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport scipy\nfrom scipy import stats\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nOUT = ROOT / \"results\"\nFIG = ROOT / \"figures\"\nOUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nFIG.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nmanifest = json.loads((ROOT / \"input/sources.json\").read_text())\nparticipants = pd.read_csv(ROOT / \"input/participants.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\")\nmap_items = [(p, x) for p, x in manifest[\"files\"].items() if p.endswith(\".nii.gz\")]\nmap_items.sort(key=lambda x: x[1][\"participant_id\"])\nids = [v[\"participant_id\"] for _, v in map_items]\nassert len(ids) == 54 and len(set(ids)) == len(ids)\nassert set(ids) == set(participants.participant_id)\nassert (participants.set_index(\"participant_id\").loc[ids, \"group\"] == \"equalIndifference\").all()\n\nimgs = [nib.load(ROOT / rel) for rel, _ in map_items]\nshape, affine = imgs[0].shape, imgs[0].affine\nassert all(im.shape == shape and np.allclose(im.affine, affine, atol=1e-5) for im in imgs)\nstack = np.stack([im.get_fdata(dtype=np.float32) for im in imgs])\nassert np.isfinite(stack).all()\n# In these effect maps, exact zero denotes no modeled voxel support. Requiring\n# support in all participant maps avoids treating uncovered voxels as zero effects.\nmask = np.all(stack != 0, axis=0)\nassert mask.sum() > 1000\nX = stack[:, mask].astype(np.float64)\nn, v = X.shape\nassert n == 54 and np.isfinite(X).all()\n\nmeans = X.mean(axis=0)\nsd = X.std(axis=0, ddof=1)\nse = sd / np.sqrt(n)\nt_obs = means / se\ndf = n - 1\np_unc = stats.t.sf(t_obs, df)\n\n# Null symmetry permits participant-level sign flips. The maximum positive t\n# across the full analysis mask controls one-sided voxelwise whole-brain FWE.\nN_PERM = 9999\nSEED = 20261016\nrng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\nsum_sq = np.square(X).sum(axis=0)\nmax_null = np.empty(N_PERM, dtype=np.float64)\nbatch = 100\nfor start in range(0, N_PERM, batch):\n    stop = min(start + batch, N_PERM)\n    signs = rng.choice(np.array([-1., 1.]), size=(stop - start, n))\n    sums = signs @ X\n    # For each sign-flipped sample: t = sum(x)/(sqrt((sum(x^2)-sum(x)^2/n)/(n-1))/sqrt(n)).\n    var = np.maximum((sum_sq[None, :] - np.square(sums) / n) / (n - 1), 0.)\n    t_perm = (sums / n) / np.sqrt(var / n)\n    max_null[start:stop] = np.max(t_perm, axis=1)\np_fwe = (1 + (max_null[:, None] >= t_obs[None, :]).sum(axis=0)) / (N_PERM + 1)\n\n# A conservative analytic Bonferroni result provides a distributional reference.\np_bonf = np.minimum(1., p_unc * v)\n\n# Descriptive, coordinate-defined vmPFC display region (MNI mm); it is not the\n# hypothesis test or a substitute for the whole-brain-corrected inference.\nijk = np.indices(shape).reshape(3, -1).T\nxyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(affine, ijk)\nroi_full = ((xyz[:, 0] >= -12) & (xyz[:, 0] <= 12) &\n            (xyz[:, 1] >= 30) & (xyz[:, 1] <= 55) &\n            (xyz[:, 2] >= -15) & (xyz[:, 2] <= 10)).reshape(shape) & mask\nroi_vals = stack[:, roi_full]\nroi_subject_means = roi_vals.mean(axis=1)\nroi_mean = float(roi_subject_means.mean())\nroi_ci = stats.t.interval(.95, n - 1, loc=roi_mean,\n                          scale=stats.sem(roi_subject_means))\nroi_t, roi_p = stats.ttest_1samp(roi_subject_means, 0., alternative=\"greater\")\n\n# Independent implementation check at fixed voxels, including a max-stat p check.\ncandidate = np.argsort(p_unc)[:3]\nchecks = []\nfor j in candidate:\n    ref_t, ref_p = stats.ttest_1samp(X[:, j], 0., alternative=\"greater\")\n    assert np.isclose(ref_t, t_obs[j], rtol=1e-10, atol=1e-10)\n    assert np.isclose(ref_p, p_unc[j], rtol=1e-10, atol=1e-12)\n    checks.append({\"flat_index\": int(np.flatnonzero(mask)[j]), \"t_script\": float(t_obs[j]),\n                   \"t_scipy\": float(ref_t), \"p_script\": float(p_unc[j]), \"p_scipy\": float(ref_p)})\ncheck_signs = np.random.default_rng(SEED + 1).choice(np.array([-1., 1.]), size=n)\ncheck_sums = check_signs @ X\ncheck_var = np.maximum((sum_sq - np.square(check_sums) / n) / (n - 1), 0.)\ncheck_t = (check_sums / n) / np.sqrt(check_var / n)\ncheck_ref_t = stats.ttest_1samp(X * check_signs[:, None], 0., axis=0).statistic\nassert np.allclose(check_t, check_ref_t, rtol=1e-10, atol=1e-10)\nassert np.isclose(check_t.max(), check_ref_t.max(), rtol=1e-10, atol=1e-10)\n\nflat_indices = np.flatnonzero(mask)\norder = np.argsort(p_fwe)\npeak_j = int(order[0])\npeak_ijk = np.unravel_index(int(flat_indices[peak_j]), shape)\npeak_xyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(affine, np.array(peak_ijk))\nsig = p_fwe <= .05\nsig_count = int(sig.sum())\nbonf_sig_count = int((p_bonf <= .05).sum())\n\ndef write_map(name: str, values: np.ndarray, fill: float = 0.) -> None:\n    arr = np.full(shape, fill, dtype=np.float32)\n    arr[mask] = values.astype(np.float32)\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(arr, affine, imgs[0].header), OUT / name)\n\nwrite_map(\"group_mean.nii.gz\", means)\nwrite_map(\"group_t.nii.gz\", t_obs)\nwrite_map(\"group_p_fwe_max_t.nii.gz\", p_fwe, 1.)\n\nvm = p_fwe <= .05\nclusters = []\nif vm.any():\n    vm_full = np.zeros(shape, dtype=bool)\n    vm_full[mask] = vm\n    from scipy.ndimage import label\n    labels, nc = label(vm_full, structure=np.ones((3, 3, 3), dtype=int))\n    t_full = np.zeros(shape, dtype=np.float64)\n    t_full[mask] = t_obs\n    for k in range(1, nc + 1):\n        pts = np.argwhere(labels == k)\n        c_xyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(affine, pts).mean(axis=0)\n        peak = pts[np.argmax(t_full[tuple(pts.T)])]\n        pxyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(affine, peak)\n        clusters.append({\"cluster\": k, \"voxels\": len(pts), \"centroid_x\": c_xyz[0], \"centroid_y\": c_xyz[1], \"centroid_z\": c_xyz[2],\n                         \"peak_x\": pxyz[0], \"peak_y\": pxyz[1], \"peak_z\": pxyz[2],\n                         \"peak_t\": t_full[tuple(peak)]})\npd.DataFrame(clusters).to_csv(OUT / \"fwe_clusters.csv\", index=False)\n\nqc = pd.DataFrame({\"participant_id\": ids,\n                   \"map_mean\": stack.reshape(n, -1).mean(axis=1),\n                   \"map_sd\": stack.reshape(n, -1).std(axis=1),\n                   \"fraction_nonzero\": (stack.reshape(n, -1) != 0).mean(axis=1),\n                   \"vmPFC_box_mean\": roi_subject_means})\nqc.to_csv(OUT / \"participant_qc.csv\", index=False)\n\nsummary = {\n    \"n_participants\": n, \"n_excluded\": 0, \"map_shape\": list(shape),\n    \"voxel_sizes_mm\": [float(z) for z in imgs[0].header.get_zooms()[:3]],\n    \"n_common_support_voxels\": int(v), \"mask_definition\": \"nonzero support in all 54 maps\",\n    \"degrees_freedom\": df, \"alternative\": \"mean > 0\", \"permutation_method\": \"participant sign-flip maximum t\",\n    \"permutations\": N_PERM, \"seed\": SEED, \"minimum_fwe_p_resolution\": 1/(N_PERM+1),\n    \"fwe_alpha\": .05, \"significant_voxels\": sig_count,\n    \"bonferroni_significant_voxels_reference\": bonf_sig_count,\n    \"peak_x_mni_mm\": float(peak_xyz[0]), \"peak_y_mni_mm\": float(peak_xyz[1]),\n    \"peak_z_mni_mm\": float(peak_xyz[2]), \"peak_mean_contrast\": float(means[peak_j]),\n    \"peak_t\": float(t_obs[peak_j]), \"peak_p_uncorrected\": float(p_unc[peak_j]),\n    \"peak_p_fwe_max_t\": float(p_fwe[peak_j]), \"peak_p_fwe_bonferroni\": float(p_bonf[peak_j]),\n    \"roi_definition_mni_box_mm\": {\"x\": [-12, 12], \"y\": [30, 55], \"z\": [-15, 10]},\n    \"roi_n_voxels\": int(roi_full.sum()), \"roi_mean_contrast\": roi_mean,\n    \"roi_mean_95ci\": [float(roi_ci[0]), float(roi_ci[1])], \"roi_t\": float(roi_t),\n    \"roi_whole_brain_fwe_significant_voxels\": int((sig & roi_full[mask]).sum()),\n    \"roi_p_one_sided_descriptive\": float(roi_p), \"scipy_reference_checks\": checks,\n    \"permutation_t_reference_max_abs_difference\": float(np.max(np.abs(check_t - check_ref_t))),\n    \"permutation_max_stat_reference_difference\": float(abs(check_t.max() - check_ref_t.max())),\n    \"age_range_years\": [int(participants.age.min()), int(participants.age.max())],\n    \"gender_counts\": {str(k): int(vv) for k, vv in participants.gender.value_counts().items()},\n    \"environment\": {\"python\": sys.version.split()[0], \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n                     \"numpy\": np.__version__, \"scipy\": scipy.__version__,\n                     \"nibabel\": nib.__version__, \"pandas\": pd.__version__, \"matplotlib\": matplotlib.__version__}}\n(OUT / \"summary.json\").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n# Figure: participant-level vmPFC box contrast estimates and MNI axial t slices.\nfig = plt.figure(figsize=(11, 7), layout=\"constrained\")\ngs = fig.add_gridspec(2, 3, width_ratios=[.9, 1, 1])\nax = fig.add_subplot(gs[:, 0])\nax.scatter(np.ones(n) + rng.normal(0, .045, n), roi_subject_means, s=18, alpha=.6,\n           color=\"#345995\", edgecolors=\"none\")\nax.errorbar([1], [roi_mean], yerr=[[roi_mean-roi_ci[0]], [roi_ci[1]-roi_mean]],\n            fmt=\"o\", color=\"#c0392b\", capsize=4, markersize=6, label=\"mean and 95% CI\")\nax.axhline(0, color=\"0.35\", lw=.8, ls=\"--\")\nax.set(xlim=(.75, 1.25), xticks=[1], xticklabels=[\"vmPFC display box\"],\n       ylabel=\"Gain effect estimate (arbitrary upstream units)\",\n       title=\"Participant means (n=54)\")\nax.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=8)\n\ntdata = np.zeros(shape, dtype=np.float32); tdata[mask] = t_obs\nsig_full = np.zeros(shape, dtype=bool); sig_full[mask] = sig\nz_cuts = [-10, 0, 10, 20]\nfor ax_slice, z_mm in zip([fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 1]), fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 2]),\n                           fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 1]), fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 2])], z_cuts):\n    k = int(np.argmin(np.abs((-78 + np.arange(shape[2]) * 2.4) - z_mm)))\n    sl = np.ma.masked_where(~mask[:, :, k], tdata[:, :, k]).T\n    im = ax_slice.imshow(sl, origin=\"lower\", extent=(-97, 97, -133, 97),\n                         cmap=\"RdBu_r\", vmin=-6, vmax=6, interpolation=\"nearest\")\n    if sig_full[:, :, k].any():\n        ax_slice.contour(np.linspace(-96, 96, shape[0]), np.linspace(-132, 96, shape[1]),\n                         sig_full[:, :, k].T.astype(float), levels=[.5],\n                         colors=[\"#7b1fa2\"], linewidths=1.4)\n    ax_slice.set(xlim=(-70, 70), ylim=(-110, 75), aspect=\"equal\",\n                 xlabel=\"MNI x (mm)\", ylabel=\"MNI y (mm)\", title=f\"Axial slice z={z_mm} mm\")\n    if z_mm in (0, 10):\n        from matplotlib.patches import Rectangle\n        ax_slice.add_patch(Rectangle((-12, 30), 24, 25, fill=False,\n                                     edgecolor=\"#00a878\", linewidth=1.2, linestyle=\"--\"))\nfig.colorbar(im, ax=fig.axes[1:], shrink=.78, label=\"One-sample t (df=53)\")\nfig.suptitle(\"Gain-modulator group effects: vmPFC summary and t map (purple = whole-brain FWE p≤.05)\", fontsize=12)\nfig.savefig(FIG / \"group_results.png\", dpi=180)\nfig.savefig(FIG / \"group_results.svg\")\nplt.close(fig)\n\nprint(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n\n--- run entry/retriever ---\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nPYTHON=${PYTHON:-/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python}\n\"$PYTHON\" scripts/retrieve_maps.py > results/retrieval-manifest.txt\n\"$PYTHON\" scripts/group_analysis.py > results/run.stdout 2> results/run.stderr\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Retrieve manifest-listed participant maps and verify source byte identities.\"\"\"\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport urllib.request\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nmanifest = json.loads((ROOT / \"input/sources.json\").read_text())\nitems = [(p, d) for p, d in manifest[\"files\"].items() if p.endswith(\".nii.gz\")]\n\ndef fetch(item):\n    rel, info = item\n    out = ROOT / rel\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    if out.exists():\n        payload = out.read_bytes()\n    else:\n        req = urllib.request.Request(info[\"url\"], headers={\"User-Agent\": \"NARPS-group-study/1.0\"})\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=90) as response:\n            payload = response.read()\n        out.write_bytes(payload)\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n    ok = len(payload) == info[\"bytes\"] and digest == info[\"sha256\"]\n    if not ok:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{rel}: bytes={len(payload)} sha256={digest}; manifest mismatch\")\n    return rel, len(payload), digest\n\nwith concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as pool:\n    results = list(pool.map(fetch, items))\nfor row in results:\n    print(*row)\nprint(f\"verified {len(results)} maps; {sum(row[1] for row in results)} bytes\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
