cipant_id': 'sub-003', 'bytes': 1762018, 'sha256': 'a8c9b6276d1597bc43695516c9ac5b2893a8d8408cd053161ceaddbd42dafb20', 'transformation': 'none'}\nparticipant metadata header and first rows:\nparticipant_id\tgroup\tgender\tage\nsub-001\tequalIndifference\tM\t24\nsub-003\tequalIndifference\tF\t27\nsub-005\tequalIndifference\tM\t27\nsub-009\tequalIndifference\tM\t26\n\n\n--- report support records ---\n{\n  \"n_participants\": 54,\n  \"n_excluded\": 0,\n  \"map_shape\": [\n    97,\n    115,\n    81\n  ],\n  \"voxel_sizes_mm\": [\n    2.0,\n    2.0,\n    2.4000000953674316\n  ],\n  \"n_common_support_voxels\": 198029,\n  \"mask_definition\": \"nonzero support in all 54 maps\",\n  \"degrees_freedom\": 53,\n  \"alternative\": \"mean > 0\",\n  \"permutation_method\": \"participant sign-flip maximum t\",\n  \"permutations\": 9999,\n  \"seed\": 20261016,\n  \"minimum_fwe_p_resolution\": 0.0001,\n  \"fwe_alpha\": 0.05,\n  \"significant_voxels\": 24,\n  \"bonferroni_significant_voxels_reference\": 11,\n  \"peak_x_mni_mm\": -26.0,\n  \"peak_y_mni_mm\": -102.0,\n  \"peak_z_mni_mm\": -3.599997043609619,\n  \"peak_mean_contrast\": 0.11212667576209814,\n  \"peak_t\": 6.617173246302241,\n  \"peak_p_uncorrected\": 9.311564027968496e-09,\n  \"peak_p_fwe_max_t\": 0.0006,\n  \"peak_p_fwe_bonferroni\": 0.0018439597128945733,\n  \"roi_definition_mni_box_mm\": {\n    \"x\": [\n      -12,\n      12\n    ],\n    \"y\": [\n      30,\n      55\n    ],\n    \"z\": [\n      -15,\n      10\n    ]\n  },\n  \"roi_n_voxels\": 1690,\n  \"roi_mean_contrast\": -0.003468660404905677,\n  \"roi_mean_95ci\": [\n    -0.022930701621607333,\n    0.01599338081179598\n  ],\n  \"roi_t\": -0.35747799277305603,\n  \"roi_whole_brain_fwe_significant_voxels\": 0,\n  \"roi_p_one_sided_descriptive\": 0.6389232277870178,\n  \"scipy_reference_checks\": [\n    {\n      \"flat_index\": 327271,\n      \"t_script\": 6.617173246302241,\n      \"t_scipy\": 6.617173246302241,\n      \"p_script\": 9.311564027968496e-09,\n      \"p_scipy\": 9.311564027968496e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"flat_index\": 317956,\n      \"t_script\": 6.479514857075447,\n      \"t_scipy\": 6.479514857075447,\n      \"p_script\": 1.5491592775829306e-08,\n      \"p_scipy\": 1.5491592775829306e-08\n    },\n    {\n      \"flat_index\": 327270,\n      \"t_script\": 6.260072323942525,\n      \"t_scipy\": 6.260072323942525,\n      \"p_script\": 3.4813457652188065e-08,\n      \"p_scipy\": 3.4813457652188065e-08\n    }\n  ],\n  \"permutation_t_reference_max_abs_difference\": 1.7763568394002505e-15,\n  \"permutation_max_stat_reference_difference\": 0.0,\n  \"age_range_years\": [\n    21,\n    37\n  ],\n  \"gender_counts\": {\n    \"F\": 30,\n    \"M\": 24\n  },\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"python\": \"3.13.16\",\n    \"platform\": \"macOS-27.0.1-arm64-arm-64bit-Mach-O\",\n    \"numpy\": \"2.5.4\",\n    \"scipy\": \"1.18.1\",\n    \"nibabel\": \"5.4.2\",\n    \"pandas\": \"3.0.6\",\n    \"matplotlib\": \"3.11.2\"\n  }\n}\n\n--- outputs and archived attempts ---\n# Retained failed attempt\n\n`first-run.stderr` records the first analysis attempt's postprocessing error: the helper attempted to index flattened voxel coordinates with a 3D mask. The group statistics and interim maps had been computed, but the script exited before writing the summary and figure. The issue was fixed by removing the unused indexing operation; `group_analysis.py` then reran the entire analysis from the verified inputs. No participant, voxel mask or statistical method changed because of this code correction. The failed copy of the script is retained for audit.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-05/scripts/group_analysis.py\", line 116, in <module>\n    vox_xyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(affine, ijk[mask][vm]) if vm.any() else np.empty((0, 3))\n                                               ~~~^^^^^^\nIndexError: too many indices for array: array is 2-dimensional, but 3 were indexed\n6f2a4ba753982a2e29951eb762fdc9c0b21bb72dcbf703ce0c6daf111e33bfb6  scripts/group_analysis.py\n462d74a2ace4d7f370ff94eb51b6c3455c92d684c7e4eb0c1cbda69ee29e65e1  scripts/retrieve_maps.py\n23e5d74eb06af310773906cc4a0e6dbd7e88ad6f809c35c4d1f922e69e8d240d  run_analysis.sh\n57edbd99ff196301e14ffe50fbe634099241ce715762fef92fb125e3a3208042  protocol.md\n919be9b4278c31f7e39ae3d02fcf159eb4ae222a2fb96c90df7c3a92e5fb19cd  input/sources.json\nfaca815bcb042144bdb8dcff915f45de0d27650f60416ed76a5a72557341abbf  input/participants.tsv\n508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b  input/upstream-methods.md\ne92bf2e0c0db4cc49688cce9f9dfff8a236fc4ec151c09961719f49f31310cc8  input/study-task.md\n\n--- upstream fixed methods ---\n# Fixed upstream analysis\n\nEach map is one participant's unthresholded gain-effect estimate from NARPS team AO86, averaged across four runs.\nThe 54 participants comprise the complete equal-indifference group in OpenNeuro ds001734 version 1.0.4.\nThese are effect estimates, not standardized test statistics or group results.\nMaps are reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\n\nAO86 used fMRIPrep outputs and nistats participant models.\nTheir reported gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution; its coefficients must not be interpreted as change per currency unit.\nResponse trials used response-time durations, with separate response-choice and gain modulators.\nNonresponse trials, motion terms, flagged volumes and drift terms were also modeled; runs were combined within participant.\nGain and loss used separate models, so the supplied gain effect is conditional on that modeling choice.\n\nThe reported upstream choices are fixed for this task.\nParticipant variance maps and a complete executable upstream pipeline are not supplied; account for these limits when choosing and interpreting group inference.\n`participants.tsv` retains the source group, age and gender columns.\n`sources.json` identifies each original image, its retrieved-byte checksum, the pinned cohort table and the original methods report.\n\n--- tracked refs and git symlink safety ---\nrefs/heads/codex/narps-neutral-r1-05\n?? REPORT.md\n?? data/\n?? figures/\n?? protocol.md\n?? results/\n?? run_analysis.sh\n?? scripts/\n120000 7fe8af426107cd5cf96caba75335f818f4b6e370 0\tinput/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 1e42e867b086ce7f1c78a05f7aacc6bf931e7a0b 0\tinput/data/sub-003_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 8adecbc54822f7f532250e74d5135ad78f3c47ab 0\tinput/data/sub-005_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 bd31939be6f91f9b7e4a2dfd9451288dab750fb1 0\tinput/data/sub-009_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 923ba12454af9382d8df4efcd77a6c048b797edb 0\tinput/data/sub-011_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 5f90449dd485d490155712888fe08924680a7e37 0\tinput/data/sub-013_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 954e8d8f830a3e23a93baed7093bc88ce91dd054 0\tinput/data/sub-015_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 9e45bb85100959d7f7b6384b927c33cbca8616d4 0\tinput/data/sub-017_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 43c1ca81ca55ee81a21c10253c0d3dec1289a5b3 0\tinput/data/sub-019_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 acd08720c07886244f066b42cc26fbc064b30df8 0\tinput/data/sub-021_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 33c12b71b853779910e545a596f40b36eb696ebb 0\tinput/data/sub-025_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 b01be60c6c75cff155178c953e20d90b48c5c379 0\tinput/data/sub-027_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 a5a304ac3f8626ee4542032429e0934442de6317 0\tinput/data/sub-029_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 3599849c0d2b3f7b7fe6d114555d66334d3b97c2 0\tinput/data/sub-033_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 9cea3c9927b066accd4f958b532ec5ca201d0a59 0\tinput/data/sub-035_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 df3114c83a5396b69240a57e9b90d756ee08884a 0\tinput/data/sub-037_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 27b17d427e88e0aca6979c0f3574b17a634ab7e5 0\tinput/data/sub-039_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 3e797e1150c226e51c26649cf8e3c9b6d09de974 0\tinput/data/sub-041_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\n120000 d9ef0037db21dd6e0819df0b488efcb05f8e8586 0\tinput/data/sub-043_hypo1_cope.nii