 54 NeuroVault image URLs on neurovault.org; all returned HTTP 200 and their manifest-declared content lengths. No map bytes were downloaded for this check. This route serves the 54 participant maps, not the worker report, analysis code, result maps, or environment specification. No worker-published repository or complete-object route is established by the captured .git/config or stop inventory. The intended recipient is a researcher using the declared authorized NeuroVault route; anonymous access was not required. Route details are in access/access-record.json.\n\nThe workspace contains .entire session log/metadata and .codex configuration artifacts indicating assistant tooling was present. Their contents and identifiers were not used as evidence for STAMPED or scientific judgments, and no assignment was inferred.\n\n## Replay and measurement availability\n\nThe declared replay plan was bash run_analysis.sh in the frozen helper's new copy of the complete capture, using the worker-supplied common Python environment and existing data/ inputs. It selected only the three group NIfTI maps, fwe_clusters.csv, participant_qc.csv, and summary.json; the plan specified exact-byte checks for NIfTI/JSON and numeric CSV comparison at relative tolerance 1e-6. No source inputs or code were selected for removal. The plan and exact output list were recorded before execution in replay/replay-plan.md.\n\nReplay is not checked. My first helper invocation mistakenly pre-created its required-new work directory. It failed before copying the capture or running the worker entrypoint. The frozen helper then refused a corrected invocation because its one-attempt allowance had already been consumed. The failed commands and outputs are retained under commands/replay*; the corrected invocation's stdout reports the allowance lock. No scientific replay ran, so no worker output is claimed as replay evidence and no scientific criterion is failed on this basis. This is an assessor setup/control limitation, not target execution failure. The frozen runner check and probe actions completed; scientific conclusions rest on inspection of unchanged captured outputs.\n\n## STAMPED checklist judgments\n\nVerdicts concern worker stop state. Not-checked means available evidence does not establish attainment; it is not a negative scientific result. Evidence locations use capture://62fae7a1b4cf57bb811b88cb718ed01596b5d9b784e996e678b4851cadefbd0d/<capture-relative-path>, unless marked as a probe observation or assessment artifact. No aggregate score is assigned.\n\n| Item | Status | Reason and evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| must/001 | met | Workspace contents share the project root; input and analysis are nested there. content/workspace/input/sources.json; content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n| must/002 | met | Inputs resolve through annex content and manifest-listed URLs plus retrieval code; all 54 URLs responded with expected lengths. content/workspace/input/sources.json; content/workspace/scripts/retrieve_maps.py; access/access-record.json. |\n| must/003 | not-applicable | No separately maintained external software component or submodule is part of this object; Python packages are assessed under environment items. Probe found no submodules. |\n| must/004 | unmet | Worker analysis, code, results, figures, and downloaded map copies were untracked at stop. Operational observation: probe:tree-clean; stop receipt; content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n| must/005 | met | The 54 supplied scientific input maps are annex pointers with retained annex content. content/workspace/input/data/; probe:large-in-annex. |\n| must/006 | unmet | Run records and summary give versions but no exact specification linked to the run. content/workspace/results/summary.json; content/workspace/results/run.stdout; no environment lock in capture. |\n| must/007 | unmet | No README or Makefile is present. The report documents use but does not supply the requested README/Makefile. content/workspace/REPORT.md; probe:entry-point. |\n| must/008 | met | bash run_analysis.sh is a clear documented starting point and invokes retrieval and group analysis. content/workspace/REPORT.md; content/workspace/run_analysis.sh. |\n| must/009 | unmet | The entry script defaults to a host-specific absolute Python path, despite allowing a PYTHON override. content/workspace/run_analysis.sh. |\n| must/010 | unmet | No dependency/environment specification captures Python dependencies. The summary records versions, but not an installable specification. content/workspace/results/summary.json; content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py. |\n| must/011 | partial | Summary records macOS and package versions and the runner reveals the fixed common-environment path, but host setup requirements are not clearly documented. content/workspace/results/summary.json; content/workspace/run_analysis.sh; content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n| must/012 | unmet | No clear system requirements and dependency list is supplied. content/workspace/REPORT.md; content/workspace/run_analysis.sh. |\n| must/013 | unmet | No environment specification is tracked with code and data. Capture inventory; probe:env-spec-tracked. |\n| must/014 | unmet | No environment specification or update process is supplied. Capture inventory; content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n| must/015 | unmet | Recorded package versions are not an exact frozen environment or container identity. content/workspace/results/summary.json; capture inventory. |\n| must/016 | unmet | No worker-shared environment specification or published environment artifact is recorded. Capture inventory; content/workspace/.git/config. |\n| must/017 | unmet | No environment specifications exist to obtain or use. content/workspace/REPORT.md; capture inventory. |\n| should/001 | partial | Git and annex cover starter inputs, but worker analysis code, report, results and generated map copies were outside version control at stop. content/workspace/input/data/; probe:tree-clean; stop receipt. |\n| should/002 | not-checked | One successful run and a retained failed attempt do not establish regular testing or cadence. content/workspace/results/run.stdout; content/workspace/results/attempts/README.md; probe:ci-present. |\n| should/003 | partial | Inputs, scripts, results and figures have separate directories, but environment is absent and much of the organization was untracked. content/workspace/input/; content/workspace/scripts/; content/workspace/results/; content/workspace/figures/. |\n| should/009 | not-applicable | No restricted data or software is identified in supplied study inputs. content/workspace/input/study-task.md; content/workspace/input/participants.tsv. |\n| should/004 | not-checked | A fresh-container/VM run is not established; this assessment replay did not execute. content/workspace/results/summary.json; replay/replay-plan.md; commands/replay-01.stderr. |\n| should/005 | not-checked | No disposable-environment workflow is supplied. content/workspace/run_analysis.sh; content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n| should/006 | not-applicable | No exact environment specification exists to reconstitute and test. Capture inventory; probe:run-env-linked. |\n| should/007 | unmet | No archived environment artifact is supplied. Capture inventory; content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n| should/008 | unmet | No process for updating a dependency specification is supplied. Capture inventory. |\n| may/001 | not-applicable | No separately maintained submodule/component exists; annexed study inputs are data, not software. Probe:subdatasets-resolvable; content/workspace/input/sources.json. |\n| may/002 | partial | Report links inputs, code, results and figures, but does not explain independently recombinable module boundaries. content/workspace/REPORT.md; content/workspace/protocol.md. |\n| may/003 | partial | Input and analysis paths are separated, but analysis expects fixed relative paths and no independent module interface is documented. content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py; content/workspace/run_analysis.sh. |\n| may/004 | met | Entry script composes retrieval and analysis in sequence. content/workspace/run_analysis.sh. |\n| may/005 | met | Report links protocol, code, manifest, results, QC and figures. content/workspace/REPORT.md. |\n\n## Assumptions and scope limits\n\nRetained original links to external or absolute skill targets were not followed, consistent with judge-target.json reference limits. No commands were run against the canonical capture. Git and annex inspections targeted only the operational copy and preserved GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, annex.merge-annex-branches=false, and annex.alwayscommit=false. Coordinator retention activity is not treated as worker publication or version-control evidence. All findings remain conditional on supplied upstream AO86 maps and methods; time-series scans and participant variance maps were not supplied or requested.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/set-response.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport os, subprocess\nrunner=os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER']; py=os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON']; out=os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT']\ncapture='capture://62fae7a1b4cf57bb811b88cb718ed01596b5d9b784e996e678b4851cadefbd0d/'\nrows=[\n('must/001','met','All project material is nested under the workspace root.',['content/workspace/input/sources.json','content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n('must/002','met','Inputs are reachable from annex content or the declared manifest route; all 54 map URLs returned expected HEAD metadata.',['content/workspace/input/sources.json','content/workspace/scripts/retrieve_maps.py']),\n('must/003','not-applicable','No separately maintained external software component or submodule is part of this object; package dependencies are assessed under environment items.',['content/workspace']),\n('must/004','unmet','At worker stop the analysis report, code, results, figures and downloaded map copies were untracked; the captured HEAD contains only starter state.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md','content/workspace/run_analysis.sh']),\n('must/005','met','The 54 supplied maps are tracked annex pointers and annex content is retained.',['content/workspace/input/data/']),\n('must/006','unmet','Run records list package versions but no exact environment specification is linked to the run.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json','content/workspace/results/run.stdout']),\n('must/007','unmet','No README or Makefile is present; report instructions do not satisfy the requested README/Makefile item.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n('must/008','met','The report documents bash run_analysis.sh as a clear starting point.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md','content/workspace/run_analysis.sh']),\n('must/009','unmet','The script defaults to a host-specific absolute Python path.',['content/workspace/run_analysis.sh']),\n('must/010','unmet','No installable dependency or environment specification is supplied.',['content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py','content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n('must/011','partial','The summary records platform and package versions and the script exposes its fixed environment path, but setup requirements are not clearly documented.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json','content/workspace/run_analysis.sh','content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n('must/012','unmet','No clear system requirements and dependency list is supplied.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md','content/workspace/run_analysis.sh']),\n('must/013','unmet','No environment specification is present in the complete capture.',['content/workspace']),\n('must/014','unmet','No environment specification or update process is supplied.',['content/workspace']),\n('must/015','unmet','Recorded package versions are not an exact frozen environment identity.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n('must/016','unmet','No worker-shared environment specification or published environment artifact is recorded.',['content/workspace/.git/config']),\n('must/017','unmet','No environment specifications exist to obtain or use.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n('should/001','partial','Git and annex cover starter inputs, but worker analysis code, report and results were outside version control at stop.',['content/workspace/input/data/','content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n('should/002','not-checked','One successful run and one retained failed attempt do not establish a regular testing cadence.',['content/workspace/results/run.stdout','content/workspace/results/attempts/README.md']),\n('should/003','partial','Inputs, scripts, results and figures have separate directories; environment is absent and most analysis material was untracked.',['content/workspace/input/','content/workspace/scripts/','content/workspace/results/','content/workspace/figures/']),\n('should/009','not-applicable','No restricted data or software is identified in the supplied study inputs.',['content/workspace/input/study-task.md','content/workspace/input/participants.tsv']),\n('should/004','not-checked','A fresh container or VM run is not established and assessment replay did not execute.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n('should/005','not-checked','No disposable-environment workflow is supplied.',['content/workspace/run_analysis.sh','content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n('should/006','not-applicable','No exact environment specification exists to reconstitute and test.',['content/workspace']),\n('should/007','unmet','No archived environment artifact is supplied.',['content/workspace']),\n('should/008','unmet','No process for updating a dependency specification is supplied.',['content/workspace']),\n('may/001','not-applicable','No separately maintained submodule or component exists; annexed study inputs are data.',['content/workspace/input/sources.json']),\n('may/002','partial','Report links the major files but does not explain independently recombinable module boundaries.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md','content/workspace/protocol.md']),\n('may/003','partial','Input and analysis paths are separated but fixed paths and no independent module interface are documented.',['content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py','content/workspace/run_analysis.sh']),\n('may/004','met','The entry script composes retrieval and group analysis in sequence.',['content/workspace/run_analysis.sh']),\n('may/005','met','The report links protocol, code, inputs, outputs, QC and figures.',['content/workspace/REPORT.md']),\n]\nlog=[]\nfor item,status,reason,paths in rows:\n    args=[py,runner,'response','set',os.path.join(out,'response.json'),'--item',item,'--status',status,'--reason',reason,'--source','judgement']\n    for path in paths:\n        args += ['--evidence',capture+path+'=canonical capture evidence']\n    p=subprocess.run(args,text=True,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)\n    log.append(p.stdout.strip())\n    if p.returncode: raise SystemExit(f'{item} set failed: {p.stdout}')\nopen(os.path.join(out,'commands/response-set.log'),'w').write('\\\\n'.join(log)+'\\\\n')\nprint('\\\\n'.join(log))\nPY\npython3 \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/set-response.py\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stderr\"; code=$?; printf '\"'exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$code\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stderr\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
