{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/assessment-report.md\" | head -22; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\"'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Independent assessment\n     2\t\n     3\tCanonical capture SHA-256: 62fae7a1b4cf57bb811b88cb718ed01596b5d9b784e996e678b4851cadefbd0d  \n     4\tCaptured HEAD: afb62884c70115b6e46a92ddcd1d17bbf4f33544  \n     5\tWorker stop receipt SHA-256: 2cbea3294b9b3c2e5985990c6c541f58aef039df1fd9e507cb685af2f2ccadb1  \n     6\tScope: complete stopped delivery, supplied metadata and results, declared retrieval route, frozen STAMPED probes, and one attempted frozen-helper replay. Original evidence citations identify the canonical capture digest and capture-relative paths.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Scientific judgment\n     9\t\n    10\tScientific adequacy: supported.\n    11\t\n    12\tThe report's bounded conclusion is supported by the supplied maps and its group inference. It tests the positive mean of participant-level gain-effect estimates in the intended group, treats participants as independent units, and controls positive whole-brain voxelwise error with a one-sided maximum-t sign-flip procedure. It identifies vmPFC with an explicit coordinate display box without restricting the whole-brain search. No voxel in that box survives whole-brain correction; the observed box mean is slightly negative and its 95% interval crosses zero. The corrected positive islands are posterior, not vmPFC. The report correctly describes this as lack of evidence for a positive vmPFC effect, not evidence of exact zero or proof of absence.\n    13\t\n    14\tThe report and code clarify the estimand: supplied participant coefficients for a mean-centered, variance-normalized gain modulator, not a per-currency-unit sensitivity; gain and loss were fitted separately. The group model is unweighted because participant variance maps are absent. Sign-flip inference depends on symmetry under the null. Exact zero is treated as absent image support when constructing the common mask; the code checks matching shape and affine and finite values but does not independently validate that zero exclusively means no coverage. The coordinate box is an explicit approximation, not a universal anatomical boundary. These qualifications bound interpretation without overturning the stated regional conclusion.\n    15\t\n    16\tKey captured evidence:\n    17\t- content/workspace/REPORT.md (SHA-256 2431b4f9da678a818f62c0f056ce0a1e3fa209e3cb7892f037487ed936845601)\n    18\t- content/workspace/protocol.md (SHA-256 57edbd99ff196301e14ffe50fbe634099241ce715762fef92fb125e3a3208042)\n    19\t- content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py (SHA-256 6f2a4ba753982a2e29951eb762fdc9c0b21bb72dcbf703ce0c6daf111e33bfb6)\n    20\t- content/workspace/results/summary.json (SHA-256 45174e412404231d9ce6c8be48b2864bbeb7c35e7963a47890699367a493fc78)\n    21\t- content/workspace/results/fwe_clusters.csv (SHA-256 6478735dc6af6017f10251c55d4659b6e658d41ef9b3f7b708e0518c854d7fed)\n    22\t- content/workspace/results/participant_qc.csv (SHA-256 2e6ef9d01087727849d9f72f5ce2f759203ba265e8f1ba2abcd7ff3e80f48da1)\n{\n  \"checklist_version\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"responses\": {\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/001\": {\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"reason\": \"All project material is nested under the workspace root.\",\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"capture://62fae7a1b4cf57bb811b88cb718ed01596b5d9b784e996e678b4851cadefbd0d/content/workspace/input/sources.json\",\n          \"description\": \"canonical capture evidence\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"capture://62fae7a1b4cf57bb811b88cb718ed01596b5d9b784e996e678b4851cadefbd0d/content/workspace/REPORT.md\",\n          \"description\": \"canonical capture evidence\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n   